  "category": "tradeoff",
  "question": "In the episode on why AI products fail, what tradeoff do Kiriti Badam and Aishwarya Naresh Reganti recommend when teams first deploy an AI agent—what do they gain by keeping autonomy low, and what do they defer?",
  "expected_points": [
    "Start with high human control and low autonomy to clarify the problem and manage risks.",
    "Defer more autonomous, complex capabilities until later."
  ],
  "evidence_quote": "when you start with building a very minimalistic version with high human control and low agency, it also forces you to think about what is the problem that I'm going to solve.",
